 {t:'1. Walking around',pv:'walk',h:`<p>You are the astronaut on the map. Move around the base:</p>
<p>${kc('W')}${kc('A')}${kc('S')}${kc('D')} or the arrow keys ${kc('◀')}${kc('▲')}${kc('▼')}${kc('▶')}</p>
<p><b>On a phone or tablet?</b> Hold the on-screen arrows. Outside, tap Sprint or hold Shift for longer, faster bounds. Let the sprint meter refill. The pocket map marks your suit in amber and stations in blue.</p>
<p><b>Jump!</b> Press ${kc('Space')} (or the <b>Jump</b> button) to hop. The Moon’s gravity is only about 1/6 of Earth’s, so you float for a long time.</p>
<div class="tip">Walls and buildings are solid. Use the door in the middle of the habitat to go in and out.</div>
<div class="tip"><b>Lunar rover:</b> if you installed it in the Equipment lab, you drive it automatically outside at double walking speed while its battery lasts. When the battery is empty it stays parked and recharges at the base overnight. Rovers can’t jump.</div>`},
 {t:'2. Using buildings',pv:'use',h:`<p>Walk close to a building. The <b style="color:var(--ice)">blue hint line</b> under the map tells you what it does.</p>
<p>Then press ${kc('E')} (or tap the orange <b>Use</b> button) to do it.</p>
<p><b>Shortcut:</b> tap an action card to walk to its station. Steer to cancel. Power and crew time are spent on arrival.</p>
<div class="tip">Greyed-out cards mean you don’t have enough power or crew time for that action right now.</div>`},
 {t:'3. What you can do',h:`<ul>
<li><b>Make air:</b> the air plant (bottom right outside) refills air. It is stronger at a crater rim with ice.</li>
<li><b>Grow food:</b> greenhouse (top right outside). Lamps use power.</li>
<li><b>Moon walk: science:</b> the sample site (bottom left). You need 5 walks to win, but it adds radiation dose.</li>
<li><b>Pile moon dirt:</b> at the northern supply depot. Moon dirt (regolith) shields the habitat from storms.</li>
<li><b>Call Earth:</b> inside at COMMS. Learn if tomorrow is stormy, but the signal takes time.</li>
<li><b>Door:</b> enter or leave the habitat. <b>Your bunk:</b> sleep and end the day.</li></ul><div class="tip">Each of the 5 jobs opens a short <b>mini-game</b>. Do well for a bigger payoff. You can skip, but the result is weaker.</div>`},
 {t:'4. Your four meters',h:`<div class="legend">
<span class="sw" style="background:#f2d03a"></span><span><b>POWER</b>: solar panels charge your battery on sunny days. Actions use it up.</span>
<span class="sw" style="background:#6ad4ea"></span><span><b>AIR</b>: you breathe 10 every day. Zero means game over.</span>
<span class="sw" style="background:#6fd08c"></span><span><b>FOOD</b>: you eat about 8 every day. Zero means game over.</span>
<span class="sw" style="background:#ef5b5b"></span><span><b>DOSE</b>: radiation your body has absorbed. It only goes up, and 100 means game over.</span></div>
<div class="tip">Under the map you also see <b>Crew time</b> (●●●) and your <b>Science</b> count out of 5.</div>`},
 {t:'5. How a day works',h:`<ul>
<li>Each day you have <b>3 crew time</b> dots. Every action costs 1 dot and some power.</li>
<li>When you’re done, walk to your bunk or press <b>End the day</b>. You use 10 air, about 8 food and 3 power just to stay alive.</li>
<li>Watch the banner above the meters:</li></ul>
<div class="tip warn"><b>⚠ Solar storm:</b> going outside gives a huge dose. Stay inside, and pile moon dirt beforehand to cut the damage.</div>
<div class="tip"><b>🌙 Lunar night</b> (every 4th day): no sunlight, so your battery does all the work. Charge up first.</div>`},
 {t:'You’re ready!',h:`<p><b>Quick tips:</b></p><ul>
<li>Use <b>Call Earth</b> to peek at tomorrow’s storm, then plan around it.</li>
<li>Build shielding <i>before</i> a storm, not during.</li>
<li>If power hits zero, air drains faster. Don’t let it.</li>
<li>Each survived night unlocks <b>2 Tech Parts</b> from supplies on site. Each of your first five science walks releases one more part at the next overnight review. Excellent mini-games earn an end-of-mission bonus. Spend them in the <b>Equipment lab</b> before launch or in the habitat to upgrade the air plant, greenhouse, shelter, suits and solar field.</li></ul>
<div class="tip">The “Did you know?” boxes are real NASA science facts. Sources are listed at the bottom of the page under <b>Where the science comes from</b>.</div>`}
];
let tIdx=0,tOpen=false;
const tc=document.createElement('canvas');tc.width=32;tc.height=32;tc.className='pv';
function renderTut(){
 const st=TSTEPS[tIdx];
 $('tdots').innerHTML=TSTEPS.map((_,i)=>`<i class="${i==tIdx?'on':''}"></i>`).join('');
 $('tutBody').innerHTML=`<h2 class="px">${st.t}</h2>`+(st.pv?'<div id="pvslot"></div>':'')+st.h;
 if(st.pv)$('pvslot').appendChild(tc);
 $('tback').disabled=tIdx==0;
 $('tnext').textContent=tIdx==TSTEPS.length-1?'Let’s go!':'Next ▶';
 $('tskip').style.display=tIdx==TSTEPS.length-1?'none':'block';
}
function openTut(){tIdx=0;tOpen=true;for(const k in K)K[k]=0;$('tut').classList.remove('hidden');renderTut();requestAnimationFrame(tutLoop)}
function closeTut(){tOpen=false;$('tut').classList.add('hidden');try{localStorage.setItem(TUT_KEY,'1')}catch(e){}}
function tutLoop(t){
 if(!tOpen)return;
 const c=tc.getContext('2d');c.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;
 c.fillStyle='#8f8f8b';c.fillRect(0,0,32,32);
 for(let i=0;i<14;i++){c.fillStyle=i%2?'rgba(0,0,0,.14)':'rgba(255,255,255,.14)';c.fillRect((i*11)%30,(i*7)%30,3,1)}
 const st=TSTEPS[tIdx];
 if(st.pv=='walk'){const dir=[2,1,0,3][((t/900)|0)%4];MapArt.drawPlayer(c,16,15,dir,1,t)}
 else if(st.pv=='use'){c.fillStyle='#59627c';c.fillRect(18,6,12,14);c.fillStyle='#6ad4ea';c.fillRect(20,8,8,3);
  const k=(t/700)%2<1;if(k){c.fillStyle='#f2a23a';c.fillRect(21,3,6,1)}
  MapArt.drawPlayer(c,10,20,1,0,t)}
 else MapArt.drawPlayer(c,16,15,2,0,t);
 requestAnimationFrame(tutLoop)}
$('help').onclick=openTut;$('howto').onclick=openTut;
$('tnext').onclick=()=>{if(tIdx<TSTEPS.length-1){tIdx++;renderTut()}else closeTut()};
